# x is never assigned, so the bound is asked for every initial x; x is compared only with
# integers, so it is an integer, no state satisfies 0 < x and x < 1, and c stays 0.
# Expected: valid.  Read with x a real, the guard held at x = 1/2 and the answer was unknown.
c := 0;
if 0 < x and x < 1 {
	c := 1
}
return c
?Ex[c] <= 0
